From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 03:37:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: bypass HQoS for rate-uncapped PPPQ flows

The MT7988 HQoS engine has an aggregate ~10 Gbps end-to-end cap that
bottlenecks multi-10G SKUs even when no shaping is configured. When
the egress PPPQ has MTK_QTX_SCH_MAX_RATE_EN clear, leave IB2 QID,
PSE_QOS, and TPORT_IDX at zero so the flow skips HQoS entirely. New
helper mtk_queue_has_rate_cap() handles the netsys v3 vs MT7988 register
layout split; flows are re-stamped automatically when
mtk_set_queue_speed() later programs a cap.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c     |   17 ++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h     |    2 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c |   17 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -900,6 +900,23 @@ out:
 	mtk_w32(eth, val, soc->reg_map->qdma.qtx_sch + ofs);
 }
 
+bool mtk_queue_has_rate_cap(struct mtk_eth *eth, unsigned int idx)
+{
+	const struct mtk_soc_data *soc = eth->soc;
+	u32 val, mask;
+
+	if (!MTK_HAS_CAPS(soc->caps, MTK_QDMA))
+		return false;
+
+	mtk_qdma_select_page(eth, idx);
+	val = mtk_r32(eth, soc->reg_map->qdma.qtx_sch + MTK_QTX_REG_OFS(idx));
+
+	mask = mtk_qtx_sch_is_v3_layout(eth) ? MTK_QTX_SCH_MAX_RATE_EN_V3
+					     : MTK_QTX_SCH_MAX_RATE_EN;
+
+	return !!(val & mask);
+}
+
 static void mtk_gdm_mac_link_up(struct mtk_mac *mac,
 				struct phy_device *phy,
 				unsigned int mode, phy_interface_t interface,
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -1695,4 +1695,6 @@ static inline bool mtk_qtx_sch_is_v3_lay
 	       eth->soc->caps != MT7988_CAPS;
 }
 
+bool mtk_queue_has_rate_cap(struct mtk_eth *eth, unsigned int idx);
+
 #endif /* MTK_ETH_H */
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
@@ -364,6 +364,23 @@ mtk_flow_set_output_device(struct mtk_et
 		queue = pse_port - 1;
 	}
 
+	/* On netsys v3, skipping mtk_foe_entry_set_queue() leaves IB2.PSE_QOS
+	 * and the v3 TPORT_IDX field at zero so the flow bypasses the HQoS
+	 * engine (subject to its ~10 Gbps end-to-end cap). Only stamp the
+	 * PPPQ qid when the egress data queue has a max-rate cap programmed
+	 * and therefore actually needs shaping. Applies to direct GMAC and
+	 * DSA egress alike (e.g. unshaped 10G WAN GMAC bypasses HQoS).
+	 *
+	 * Gate on the data-queue rate cap, not the ACK partner: only the
+	 * data queue is programmed by mtk_set_queue_speed() on link change,
+	 * so the ACK partner's MAX_RATE_EN_V3 bit is always 0 even when the
+	 * port is capped. Checking the ACK queue would skip the stamp for
+	 * every TCP-ACK flow on netsys v3+.
+	 */
+	if (mtk_is_netsys_v3_or_greater(eth) &&
+	    !mtk_queue_has_rate_cap(eth, queue))
+		goto out;
+
 	/* TCP ACK flows go onto the high-priority half of the PPPQ
 	 * range so they are not queued behind bulk data on the same
 	 * egress port. Applies to both DSA user ports and direct GMAC
